<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Feedback</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Read&nbsp;Below</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>A couple things here:</strong></p>
<p>The <span style="text-decoration: underline;">entire page</span> should be looked over for punctuation errors. Capitalization, commas, etc. It breaks immersion seeing a Foundation researcher write;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;by singing the song take on me by aha&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It should be:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;By singing the song Take On Me by Aha.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Revision 5159-A should be capitalized, and I highly recommend it is put in a quote box to separate it from the rest of the page.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>- Audio from Skimmers radio during investigation</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You should add who Skimmers is, before the log. I don't know if he is a government agent, an MTF officer, a scientist, etc. Example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>MTF Agent dispatched:</strong> Skimmers, John<br />
<strong>Time:</strong> 0500 Dec 16, 2020<br />
<strong>Reason for dispatch:</strong> Unknown anomalous presence</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This gives more clarity on who he is. Remember, the Foundation documents basically everything. They are trying to study these things, and these documents are looked back upon for research in the future.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> do you have a name?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5159:</strong> Yes, my name is Joseph Walker.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here personally I don't think the Foundation really cares what his name is. They view him as an anomaly, not as a person. Staff are often very cold with the SCPs unless there is an anomalous or memetic reason not to be.</p>
<p>Also don't forget your rating module. A common mistake.</p>
<p>Other than that, good job.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

