<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/longjumpingman" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7027876); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7027876&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608142424" alt="LongJumpingMan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7027876)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/longjumpingman" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7027876); return false;">LongJumpingMan</a></span>,</p>
<p>As per the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-10629348/new-draft-forum-policies">Draft Forum Policies</a>, new authors are to <strong>get their concepts reviewed and greenlighted by two experienced reviewers</strong> on the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Idea Critique Forums</a> before posting on the Draft Critique Forums.</p>
<p>During the conceptualization stage, reviewers can give assistance in developing an idea <em>before</em> a draft is written. They can also assist in letting you know if something similar exists on the site already, or inform you of various clichés/pitfalls to be cautious of. These elements are more effectively addressed earlier in the writing process.</p>
<p>If you would like to request a draft review without greenlights, you can use the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/chat-guide">IRC Chatrooms</a> to solicit critique.</p>
<p>If you have already received the requisite greenlights, please note the thread in which you received them, or the users whom provided them.</p>

