			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846379">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard Format, Testing Logs.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
- A document that may be used to physically restrain someone<br />
- If used, Person B would not be able to enter the distance provided by Person A for the stated amount of time.<br />
- Person B is physically impended by an invisible barrier.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The central narrative would be told over the testing logs, a baseline test to see how it works before certain &quot;interesting&quot; tests are done, the story here would be subtle in the notes afterwards, subjects reporting feeling safer after a certain death, etc.<br />
<strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
The testing logs will include what I believe to be unique testing logs, like what would happen if someone put their name in for both options, what would happen if the distance was set at a giant amount, etc.<br />
<strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
If people feel the story might not be clear just via notes of the testing logs, I might also include a discovery log which gives more hints (since I'd rather it not be obvious).</p>

